ns-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:27px;color:#3f4f47;mso-line-height-rule=
:exactly;">A shipment can reach the dock before its usable traceability rec=
ord does. The product is physically there. The lot references, certificates=
, event records, and receiving data that would let the next operator accept=
 it are not, or they arrive in a form the receiving system can&#x2019;t use=
. So the team rebuilds the trail by hand from inboxes, portals, and discon=
nected systems before it can decide whether to accept, hold, investigate, o=
r escalate.</p>=0A<p style=3D"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:&apos;DM Sans&apo=
s;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&apos;Segoe UI&apos;,Roboto,Helvetica,A=
rial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:27px;color:#3f4f47;mso-line-heig=
ht-rule:exactly;">Most companies can trace at least part of a product insid=
e their own environment. The harder problem starts when that history has to=
 cross into another company&#x2019;s ERP, WMS, QMS, MES, or receiving proce=
ss. Item identifiers differ. Lot and serial references don&#x2019;t match. =
Certificates travel separately from the shipment. Event records use differe=
nt structures.</p>=0A<p style=3D"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:&apos;DM Sans&=
apos;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&apos;Segoe UI&apos;,Roboto,Helvetic=
a,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:27px;color:#3f4f47;mso-line-h=
eight-rule:exactly;">NIST gave this problem a current technical foundation =
on September 9. <a href=3D"https://www.nist.gov/publications/supply-chain-t=
raceability-principles-manufacturing-meta-framework" style=3D"color:#2a6b4f=
;text-decoration:underline;">NIST IR 8536</a> lays out a manufacturing trac=
eability meta-framework for building a continuous, time-ordered provenance =
chain across separate supply chain ecosystems. It relies on common data pat=
terns, interoperable interfaces, cryptographically verifiable links, and se=
lective disclosure, so companies can share the evidence traceability requir=
es without exposing proprietary operating data or depending on a central re=
pository.</p>=0A<p style=3D"margin:0 0 26px;font-family:&apos;DM Sans&apos;=
,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&apos;Segoe UI&apos;,Roboto,Helvetica,Ari=
al,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:27px;color:#3f4f47;mso-line-height=
-rule:exactly;">The framework matters less than what it signals for operato=
rs. The shift is from visibility to usability. A supplier can hold the righ=
t information and still fail the handoff if the receiver can&#x2019;t conne=
ct it to the product, lot, shipment, event, or decision inside its own work=
flow. Traceability is becoming part of the supplier handshake, judged along=
side the product, the ASN, and the delivery date.</p>=0A<table role=3D"pres=
entation" cellspacing=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"0" border=3D"0" width=3D"100%" s=
